{
  "schema": 1,
  "spec": "DESIGN.md — Vocabulary. atlas's own system vocabulary: the ids every question about a system takes, which are ES-DE's system names because that is what a frontend catalogue on the machine declares. World knowledge under CLAUDE.md's boundary rule — nothing here is read off a machine, so it is versioned and source-cited, and the loader refuses a malformed list rather than answering out of one.",
  "description": "systems: the canonical ids, in ES-DE's vocabulary, sorted. The set is a snapshot of one stated build's es_systems.xml, which is what makes membership checkable rather than an opinion: a name that file does not declare is not an id, however plausible it looks. A test parses the deployed file and asserts set-identity, so the snapshot cannot drift from the build in silence.",
  "sources": {
    "systems": "es_systems.xml as shipped by RetroDECK 0.10.9b (components/es-de/share/es-de/resources/systems/linux/es_systems.xml), read 2026-08-07: the 172 <system><name> values it declares. Commented-out blocks are not declarations and are not included."
  },
